// `use` looks for a module beside the importing file and, since C13, then in each directory of
// ZIMAN_MODULE_PATH. Without that a test could not live in a directory of its own -- the convention every
// language this one borrows from uses -- which is why the reference backend had zero unit tests while
// `ziman test` worked perfectly on a test file sitting beside production code.
//
// `calc` is NOT beside this file; it is in lib/, named only by module_path_sibling.env. `calc` itself
// then uses `helper`, which is found the same way, so a module reached through the path can import too.
use calc

fn main() {
    print(calc.add(2, 3))
    print(calc.tripled(4))
}
